  "nl_text": "The database schema, named schemabench_0006, is designed to manage user authentication, image and page management, and resource storage. It consists of 12 tables that work together to provide a comprehensive system for user authentication, page creation and translation, and resource management. The refinery_authentication_devise_roles table stores roles, each identified by a unique id and title, while the refinery_authentication_devise_users table stores user information, including username, email, password, and sign-in details. The refinery_authentication_devise_roles_users table links users to their respective roles, and the refinery_authentication_devise_user_plugins table stores additional user information, such as name and position. The refinery_images table stores image metadata, including mime type, name, size, and dimensions, while the refinery_image_translations table stores translated image alt and title text. The refinery_pages table stores page information, including parent page, path, and menu settings, and the refinery_page_parts table stores page part metadata, including slug and position. The refinery_page_part_translations and refinery_page_translations tables store translated page part and page titles, respectively. The refinery_resources table stores resource metadata, including file type, name, size, and extension, and the refinery_resource_translations table stores translated resource titles. The database enforces data integrity through primary keys, foreign keys, and unique constraints, ensuring that each table's data is consistent and accurate.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a content management system (CMS) tailored for Ruby on Rails developers. Refinery CMS is designed to create customizable and content-manageable websites efficiently by adhering to \"The Rails Way.\" It is well-suited for developers familiar with Ruby on Rails and aims to streamline the development process.\n\nObjectives\n\n- Provide an intuitive CMS for building and managing websites.\n- Simplify content creation and management with visual tools.\n- Support easy customization through extensions and plugins.\n- Facilitate secure user authentication and role management.\n- Enable seamless integration of media files and resources.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Developers: Primarily Ruby on Rails developers who will implement and customize websites using Refinery CMS.\n- Administrators: Users responsible for managing website content, structure, and user access.\n- End-users: Individuals who will interact with the front-end of websites built on Refinery CMS.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Page Management: \n   - Edit and organize pages using a visual editor.\n   - Manage site structure and navigation.\n\n2. Media Management:\n   - Upload and insert images seamlessly using Dragonfly.\n   - Store media on Amazon S3 for scalability.\n   - Manage and link to various resources such as PDF documents.\n\n3. User Authentication & Roles:\n   - Manage user access and roles using Devise.\n   - Define permissions for extensions and functionalities per user.\n\n4. Extension Support:\n   - Generate custom extensions using the Refinery extension generator.\n   - Popular extensions include:\n     - Blog: Manage posts, categories, and comments.\n     - Portfolio: Create image galleries.\n     - News: Post and manage news items.\n     - Inquiries: Handle contact form submissions and notifications.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Ease of Use: Designed to be approachable for Ruby on Rails developers, leveraging Rails conventions.\n- Scalability: Supports scalable media storage with Amazon S3 integration.\n- Security: Secure authentication and role management using industry-standard practices (Devise).\n- Extensibility: Easily extensible through generators and available plugins.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0006.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0006\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_authentication_devise_roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_authentication_devise_users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `sign_in_count` int(11) DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `email` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_authentication_devise_roles_users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `role_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_authentication_devise_roles_users_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_authentication_devise_users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_authentication_devise_roles_users_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_authentication_devise_roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_authentication_devise_user_plugins` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_authentication_devise_user_plugins_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_authentication_devise_users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_images` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `mime_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `size` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `width` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `height` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_image_translations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `image_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `alt` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_image_translations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`image_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_images` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_pages` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `parent_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `menu` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_pages_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_pages` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_page_parts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `page_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_page_parts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`page_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_pages` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_page_part_translations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `page_part_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_page_part_translations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`page_part_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_page_parts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_page_translations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `page_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_page_translations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`page_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_pages` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_resources` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `file_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `size` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `extension` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_resource_translations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `resource_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_resource_translations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`resource_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_resources` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
